# .worktreeinclude — gitignored files copied into each new Claude Code worktree.
#
# Uses .gitignore syntax. A file is copied only when it BOTH matches a pattern
# here AND is gitignored AND actually exists — tracked files are never
# duplicated, and missing files are silently skipped (so unused patterns no-op).
# Docs: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/worktrees#copy-gitignored-files-into-worktrees
#
# This is a framework-agnostic React library (bring-your-own-Firebase). The
# patterns below mirror the local-secret conventions in .gitignore: if such a
# file exists locally, new worktrees inherit it automatically; until then these
# lines do nothing.
#
# NOT copied on purpose: node_modules/ and dist/ (large / generated — run
# `npm install` in each worktree; the `prepare` hook rebuilds dist/). Firebase
# Functions build output (firebase/functions-*/lib/) is likewise regenerated.

# Local environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Firebase / service-account credentials (mirrors the .gitignore secret block)
service-account.json
serviceAccountKey.json
serviceAccountKey*.json
credentials.json
